-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",173,{
[5505]="7005A958\n1\tCollect the ancient dwarf remains (total: 12)\tAncient dwarf remains can be found in Máttugard. You should collect dwarf remains for Belg Thickshanks.\n2\tAdd the dwarf remains to the forge for Belg Thickshanks\tGrámi's forge can be found at the Noble Gate in Máttugard. You should add the dwarf remains to the forge for Belg Thickshanks.\n3\tTalk to Belg Thickshanks\tBelg Thickshanks can be found at the Noble Gate in Máttugard. You should talk to Belg Thickshanks.\n",
[5506]="7006D712\n1\tComplete Ikorbân Valley missions (total: 12)\tComplete missions throughout the Ikorbân Valley. Missions can be found in Iridír in Ambarûl, Urmâkh in Imhûlar, and Ub Nishir in Urash Dâr.\n2\tCompleted\tCompleted many missions throughout the Ikorbân Valley, assisting the peoples of Shagâna.\n",
[5507]="70032BDA\n1\tDefeat White Hand Metal-worker (total: 3)\030Defeat Moria Metal-worker (total: 3)\tThe tribes of Orc have forges at the hearts of their camps, out among the ruins in the main cavern of the Redhorn Lodes. The fiercest Orcs tend the forges, to process their collected metals, and fashion armour and weapons for the rest of the rabble.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have defeated the Moria and White Hand Metal-workers.\n",
[5508]="70009E26\n1\tCollect Ambi's Red Jar\030Collect Ambi's Green Jar\030Collect Ambi's Blue Bottle\030Collect Ambi's Note\030Collect Ambi's Pack\tAmbi has given you a list of his missing items to remind you exactly what they are. Ambi can be found at the tavern in Thorin's Halls. Ambi wants you to find his missing items for him.\n2\tReturn the five items to Ambi\tHaving found all of Ambi's items, return to him at the tavern in Thorin's Halls.\n",
[5509]="70047A55\n1\tCollect Easterling orders from Orcs\tThe Orc encampment of Fushaum Gund is located on the eastern slopes of the Slag-hills. You should intercept the message-bearing Orcs.\n2\tCollect orders from Orcs (total: 6)\tThe Orc encampment of Fushaum Gund is located on the eastern slopes of the Slag-hills. You should intercept the message-bearing Orcs.\n3\tShow the orders to Thurindol\tThurindol can be found at a small Ranger outpost hidden in the Slag-hills. You should show the orders to Thurindol.\n4\tBring the orders to Candúr\tCandúr can be found at a small Ranger outpost hidden in the Slag-hills. You should bring the orders to Candúr.\n5\tTalk to Thurindol\tThurindol can be found at a small Ranger outpost hidden in the Slag-hills. You should talk to Thurindol.\n",
[5510]="70041A48\n1\tDefeat Akimun\030Defeat Ralthat\030Defeat Kuri\tThe three captains can be found throughout Hata Kebir. Jajax has asked you to aid him in seeking vengeance against the captains in Hata Kebir.\n2\tTalk to Jajax\tJajax can be found at your side or called with your horn. You have defeated the three captains of Harad and should now speak to Jajax.\n",
[5511]="7006749C\n1\tReturn the goblin bandanas to Tagar\030Collect goblin bandanas ([see journal]/16)\tThe goblin encampment of Súlstrok is found to the south-east of Jax Phanâl at the foot of the mountains. Most goblins there wear bandanas. Collect the bandanas and return them to Tagar.\n",
[5512]="70019176\n1\tGather birch-wood (total: 5)\030Gather stone (total: 5)\tThere is a high concentration of birch north-east of Cerin Amroth. Stone is east, in a clearing carpeted in yellow flowers, in Gelirdor. Thavronwë has asked that you gather stone and wood for him.\n2\tReturn to Thavronwë\030Collect Birch-wood (total: 5)\030Collect Stone (total: 5)\tThavronwë is atop the flet in Cerin Amroth. You should return to Thavronwë and give him the raw materials you fetched for him.\n",
[5513]="700017AA\n1\tDefeat Krithmog\tKrithmog is somewhere within Fornost in the North Downs. If Krithmog has been returned to life and taken to Fornost he will be found somewhere where the Wargs are plentiful. Place the collar in a suitable location, then spring your trap upon him. Will Widdup named the collar as the ancient binding of Krithmog and sent you in search of a place to offer it to the revived Warg-king.\n2\tReturn the collar to Will Widdup\030Collect Krithmog's Collar\tWill Widdup is at the Treasure Hunters' Camp, in the northern North Downs. Will Widdup awaits news of your battle against Krithmog.\n",
[5514]="7000173D\n1\tDefeat Zanthrug\tAn Uruk-general was spotted entering Fornost, where he set up camp near the Great Fountain in the courtyard. Daisy Harbrook warns that the fountain has likely been desecrated and turned into an idol to Sauron. Daisy Harbrook advised you to place armour she gave you somewhere near the fountain in order to challenge the Uruk-general.\n2\tSpeak with Daisy Harbrook\030Collect Uruk-breastplate\tDaisy Harbrook awaits your return at the Free Peoples' Camp outside of Fornost. You have proven victorious over the second Uruk-general. You should return to Daisy Harbrook at once with news of your success.\n",
[5515]="7002D5D9\n1\tDefeat Angmar guards ([see journal]/6)\tThe Angmarim are in the final tower of Fornost.\n",
[5516]="7002D569\n1\tDefeat Brogadan, Wraith of Fire\tBrogadan, Wraith of Fire, is awaiting you in the third tower of Fornost.\n",
[5517]="70008087\n1\tFind Riamul and release his spirit\tRiamul is somewhere within Fornost. Emma Slee has asked you to seek the shade-captain, Riamul, and bring him word of his pardon. She hopes that his freedom will allow his men to follow.\n2\tTalk to Emma Slee\tEmma Slee is at the Fornost camp. Riamul, loyal to Angmar even in death, refused his pardon, believing that the Witch-king would restore him. You should return to Emma Slee and let her know you had to defeat him to free his men.\n",
[5518]="70008074\n1\tDefeat trolls (total: 20)\tTrolls can be found in Fornost, north of the Treasure Hunters' Camp. Will Widdup has challenged you to defeat a number of trolls within Fornost.\n2\tReturn to Will Widdup\tWill Widdup is at the Treasure Hunters' Camp in the north-western Fields of Fornost. You should return to Will Widdup and tell him of your success.\n",
[5519]="70008088\n1\tSearch skeletons for Restless Shades ([see journal]/40)\tThe shades Emma Slee sent you to free remain near their old skeletons in the upper areas of Fornost. Emma Slee wishes to free some of the shades of Fornost from the ancient curse binding them to Middle-earth. She hopes that as descendants of the Dúnedain of Arthedain the forgiveness of the Men of the North Downs might be enough to free the repentant shades.\n",
[5520]="7002D583\n1\tBurn idols to Sauron ([see journal]/4)\tIdols to Sauron can be found throughout the ruins of Fornost.\n",
[5521]="7002D574\n1\tDefeat Blogmal lieutenants ([see journal]/4)\tUruks can be found within the walls of Fornost.\n",
[5522]="7002D41F\n1\tDefeat Megoriath, the Wraith of Water\tMegoriath, the Wraith of Water, is awaiting you in the first tower of Fornost.\n",
[5523]="700080DA\n1\tTalk to Sara Oakheart\tSara Oakheart was apparently taken captive by the Blogmal Orcs while she was gathering wild herbs. She needs you to escort her out of Fornost.\n2\tDefeat Shiruk and Kamordî\tSara Oakheart was apparently taken captive by the Blogmal Orcs while she was gathering wild herbs. She needs you to escort her out of Fornost.\n",
[5524]="70002D55\n1\tDefeat shades and dreadmists (total: 40)\tShades can be found within the heart of Fornost. You should enter Fornost and defeat many of the dead of which Maedhrusc spoke.\n2\tReturn to Maedhrusc\tMaedhrusc is at the Treasure Hunters' Camp in north-western Fornost. You have defeated many of the evil dead roaming in Fornost and should return to Maedhrusc.\n",
[5525]="7002D5D1\n1\tDefeat Remmenaeg\tRemmenaeg, Wraith of Shadow, can be found at the peak of the final tower of Fornost.\n",
[5526]="7002D462\n1\tDefeat Rhavameldir, the Wraith of Earth\tRhavameldir, the Wraith of Earth, is awaiting you in the second tower of Fornost.\n",
[5527]="70008085\n1\tDefeat goblins in Fornost (total: 30)\030Defeat Orcs in Fornost (total: 30)\tIn order to improve Trestlebridge's chances against the armies of Angmar, Arch Widdup has asked you to enter Fornost and slay as many Orcs and goblins as you can.\n2\tTalk to Arch Widdup\tYou have dealt a serious blow to Angmar's host, and while not a complete victory, your efforts should at least lend courage to Arch Widdup.\n",
[5528]="7002D42A\n1\tDefeat dreadmists ([see journal]/30)\tDreadmists can be found within the flooded lower fields of Fornost.\n",
[5529]="700000FA\n1\tTalk to Istuienn\tIstuienn can be found outside the library in Esteldín. Halbarad suggested that you speak with Istuienn, a lore-master of the Rangers. She might know how to defeat the wraiths of Fornost.\n2\tCollect Remmenaeg's Morgul-hilt\030Collect Brogadan's Morgul-hilt\030Collect Rhavameldir's Morgul-hilt\030Collect Megoriath's Morgul-hilt\tThe morgul-hilts are in the possession of the four wraiths within Fornost. Istuienn believes that you may be able to find and recover the hilts of the four morgul-blades discussed in Laerdan's text inside the ruins of Fornost.\n3\tBring the morgul-hilts to Istuienn\tIstuienn is outside the library in Esteldín. You should bring the four morgul-hilts to Istuienn at once.\n",
[5530]="70008058\n1\tCollect arrowheads ([see journal]/20)\tYou might find hobbit arrowheads among the skeletons within Fornost, north of the Fornost camp.\n",
[5531]="7002D479\n1\tDefeat Jern-elyg ([see journal]/30)\t\n",
[5532]="7002D48D\n1\tDestroy the trebuchets ([see journal]/3)\tThe trebuchets must be destroyed for the safety of all in the plains of the Northdowns.\n",
[5533]="7000F65A\n1\tTalk to Ransroth\tBy completing this quest, you will be considered Neutral by the Lossoth of Forochel.\n",
[5534]="7000F65B\n1\tTalk to Ransroth\tBy completing this quest, you will be considered an Acquaintance of the Lossoth of Forochel.\n",
[5535]="7000F65C\n1\tTalk to Ransroth\tBy completing this quest, you will be considered a Friend of the Lossoth of Forochel.\n",
[5536]="7000F65D\n1\tTalk to Ransroth\tBy completing this quest, you will be considered an Ally of the Lossoth of Forochel.\n",
})
